    fix: reject consult with no title and no --failure as exit 2 usage error. Addresses LORE-055.
    
    lore consult with neither a title nor --failure slipped past the classify
    step with title=None, classified empty input as a no-match, and exited 0
    with "no matching runbook" — a scripting caller with a typo'd/missing flag
    silently read that as "no runbook matched". The help contract (LORE-007/009)
    requires a title unless --failure is given, so missing BOTH is a usage
    error, not a fail-open no-match: exit 2 with a concise stderr message
    naming both inputs. A VALID no-match (real text, no curated class) keeps
    the fail-open exit-0 contract unchanged, in both title and --failure modes.
    
    - lore/__main__.py: input guard at the top of _cmd_consult (failure/title
      falsy check); failure-mode rendering restored verbatim after the guard.
    - tests/test_lore055_consult_missing_input.py (new): pins both contracts
      via subprocess.run, with a RED proof (3/6 tests fail on pre-fix code).
    - tests/test_lore016_qa_audit.py: the LORE-016 test
      test_cli_consult_without_title_fail_open_exit0 pinned the OLD contract
      (missing input = fail-open exit 0) — revised to the LORE-055 contract
      (exit 2, error message), with the fail-open exit-0 contract unchanged
      for valid no-match input.
    - docs/INSTALL.md + README.md: consult section documents the required-title
      rule. CONTRIBUTING/README/INSTALL count literals synced 463 -> 469
      (scripts/test-count.txt updated; check-test-count.sh passes).
